    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6248" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Călĭdĭus</span></b> ,
		a, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the name of a Roman</i> gens. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> M. Calidius, <i>an
			orator</i>, <i>contemporary with Cicero</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Brut.
				79, 274</span></i> sqq.; <i><span class="en">id. Q. Fr. 1, 3, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 2,
			1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fam. 8, 4, 1</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Cn. Calidius, <i>a Roman knight</i>, <i>the father of a
				senator</i>, <i>plundered by Verres</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 4, 20, §
			42</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			Q. Calidius, <i>the father of</i> I., <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr.
				1, 13, 38</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 3, 25, § 63</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
